{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "mcp_tool_result", "ts": 1787741212.3146863, "tool": "get_lead_profile", "attempt": 1, "kind": "object", "keys": ["company_hs_id", "company_resolved", "contact_hs_id", "found", "profile", "warnings"], "result_preview": "{'found': True, 'profile': {'employee_id': 'E00010', 'company_id': 'C0010', 'decision_maker_flag': 'Yes', 'job_title': 'Managing Director', 'email': None, 'phone': '+1 (469) 312-6842', 'firstname': 'Govardhan', 'lastname': 'Terli', 'industry': 'HEALTHCARE', 'annual_revenue_m': '11.5', 'frequency_of_purchase': 'Monthly', 'lead_context': \"Health Catalyst (Nasdaq: HCAT) is a publicly traded healthcare intelligence company serving provider organizations with its flagship Igniteâ\\x84¢ platform, which unifies clinical, financial, and claims data into a standardized model, enabling self-service analytics, embedded AI, and faster enterprise decision-making. The company is in the middle of a significant platform transition: revenue declined roughly 12â\\x80\\x9313% year over year, driven by customer churn tied to DOS-to-Ignite migrations and the exit of lower-margin arrangements. Strategically, the Ignite platform and AI initiatives â\\x80\\x94 including Ignite Intelligence and Ignite Spark â\\x80\\x94 are characterized as modular, flexible upgrades that shorten sales cycles and expand accessibility. Ignite is built on Azure Databricks, and more than 1,000 organizations worldwide rely on Health Catalyst's offerings across hundreds of millions of patient records. Multitenancy is directly relevant here: as Health Catalyst migrates a large installed base of health system clients onto Ignite, securely isolating each tenant's clinical and financial data â\\x80\\x94 while sharing common infrastructure to control costs â\\x80\\x94 is a core architectural challenge. The Ignite architecture focuses on compute performance and cost control, with compute usage that is fully visible and adjustable so teams can allocate budgets, monitor usage in real time, and scale deliberately â\\x80\\x94 all concerns that a well-implemented multitenancy pattern in Spring directly addresses. **Opening question for the rep:** Given that Health Catalyst is actively migrating health system clients from its legacy platform onto Ignite, how is the engineering team currently handling tenant isolation and data segregation at scale across that growing customer base?\", 'voice_status': None, 'email_status': None, 'probability': '2', 'last_modified_voice': None, 'last_modified_email': '2026-08-24T13:52:37.327Z', 'company_name': 'Health Catalyst', 'industry_group': 'Healthcare Data & Analytics', 'about_us': 'Healthcare data-and-analytics company that unifies data and applies AI-powered insights to drive measurable clinical, financial, and operational improvement for provider organizations.', 'website_url': 'https://www.healthcatalyst.com'}, 'contact_hs_id': '533990588137', 'company_hs_id': '339297322741', 'company_resolved': True, 'warnings': []}"}
