{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741231.7555037, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 15326.0, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 14772, "output_tokens": 547, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 14, "source_urls": ["https://healthcatalystinc.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/health-catalyst-announces-strategic-partnership-microsoft", "https://www.healthcareittoday.com/2026/02/03/how-health-catalyst-turns-analytics-into-action-clinicians-actually-use/", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/news/has-25-recap-charting-the-path-to-healthcare-improvement", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/learn/insights/scaling-healthcare-analytics-ai", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/healthcare-analytics", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/learn/insights/introducing-healthcare-ai-health-catalyst", "https://app.himssconference.com/event/himss-2026/exhibitor/RXhoaWJpdG9yXzE5NTE4ODk=", "https://www.apexon.com/blog/2026-and-the-end-of-ai-pilots-scaling-intelligent-systems-in-hcls/", "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/12/16/2026-executive-predictions-why-the-ai-pilot-era-is-officially-over/", "https://premierinc.com/newsroom/blog/the-ai-wild-west-is-over-why-2026-is-the-year-health-systems-must-take-control", "https://blog.shi.com/next-generation-infrastructure/ai/two-billion-hours-short-why-healthcare-cant-afford-another-ai-pilot/", "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12894408/", "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.00839", "https://thinking.inc/en/industry-service/ai-in-healthcare/"], "chars": 1726, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Govardhan Terli at Health Catalyst:\n\n---\n\nHealth Catalyst is a Nasdaq-listed healthcare data and analytics company whose core proposition sits squarely at the intersection of the post's theme. More than 1,100 organizations worldwide rely on Health Catalyst's cloud-based ecosystem, including its Ignite™ platform and AI-enabled analytics, to drive outcomes. The company has been publicly vocal about the very tension the post addresses: as healthcare leaders face unprecedented decisions around revenue, cost, and quality, they turn to AI to maximize analytics — yet they struggle to implement AI into existing workflows, demonstrate ROI, and move AI efforts beyond predictive models. Health Catalyst's own product philosophy reinforces this: health systems shouldn't attempt enterprise transformation all at once; their Ignite platform is modular so organizations can start small, prove value, and expand into broader clinical, financial, and operational domains. This maps directly onto the broader industry moment — from mid-2025 onwards, the message to healthcare IT and data leaders has been consistent: 2026 is not about proving that AI works, but proving it works at scale, under real operational pressure, with clear financial and clinical value. Health Catalyst also recently announced a strategic partnership with Microsoft, building on Azure and Azure AI Foundry to drive reliable insight and sustained outcomes for care providers. A strong opening question for the rep: When Health Catalyst's own clients reach the end of a successful AI pilot on Ignite, what does the internal governance and change-management process look like to move that pilot into enterprise-wide adoption?"}
