{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-ff3acbe0007e", "event": "model_request", "ts": 1787741239.4299138, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "max_tokens": 2000, "search_enabled": true, "search_tool": "web_search_20250305", "search_max_uses": 5, "timeout_s": 90, "prompt_chars": 713, "system_chars": 1496, "endpoint": "anthropic.messages.create", "sent_keys": ["max_tokens", "messages", "model", "system", "tools"], "model_configured": "", "allowed_domains": [], "blocked_domains": [], "system_preview": "# Research prompt — lead_context\n\nYou are the Research Agent for a B2B lead-qualification system. You produce ONE\nshort note that will be stored on a HubSpot contact as `lead_context` and read\nlater by an email agent writing first-touch outreach.\n\n## What you are given\n\n- **The lead**: name, job title, the company they work for, and its industry.\n- **The published post**: a summary of an article our side just published.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Search the web for what is currently true about **this company** and **this\n   industry**, focused on the themes in the published post.\n2. Write a note that connects the post's themes to that specific company's\n   situation — what they actually do, how the theme lands for them, and the one\n   question a salesperson could open with.\n\n## Rules\n\n- **Ground every claim.** If the search did not support it, do not write it.\n  No invented funding rounds, headcounts, customers, or product names.\n- **Be specific to this company.** A note that would read identically for any\n  company in the industry is a failed note.\n- **Never address the lead directly** and never write email copy. This is\n  context *for* the writer, not the message itself.\n- Target ~160 words, one paragraph, plain prose — no headings, no\n  bullet lists, no markdown.\n- End with one open question a rep could ask, phrased for a first conversation.\n- If the search finds little about the company, say so plainly and stay at the\n  industry level rather than padding with generic claims.\n", "prompt_preview": "Research this lead and write the lead_context note.\n\n## The lead\n- Name: Govardhan Terli\n- Job title: Managing Director\n- Company: Health Catalyst\n- Industry: HEALTHCARE\n- Company website: https://www.healthcatalyst.com\n- About the company: Healthcare data-and-analytics company that unifies data and applies AI-powered insights to drive measurable clinical, financial, and operational improvement for provider organizations.\n\n## The post we published\n- Industry: HEALTHCARE\n- Published: 2030-01-01T00:00:00Z\n- Summary:\nA successful AI pilot in healthcare.\n\n## Your task\nSearch the web for what is true right now about Health Catalyst and the HEALTHCARE industry, focused on the themes above. Then write the note."}
{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741251.7739336, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 15067.7, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 16779, "output_tokens": 565, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 16, "source_urls": ["https://hitconsultant.net/2025/04/08/transcarent-completes-merger-with-accolade/", "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/digital-health/transcarent-completes-621m-merger-accolade", "https://transcarent.com/press-releases/transcarent-completes-merger-with-accolade", "https://transcarent.com/press-releases/transcarent-to-acquire-accolade", "https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/transcarent-finalizes-merger-accolade", "https://medcitynews.com/2025/01/accolade-transcarent-acquisition/", "https://modern-counsel.com/2025/mergers-ai-integration-and-one-place-for-health-and-care-at-transcarent/", "https://hlth.com/insights/news/transcarent-completes-merger-with-accolade-2025-04-14", "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/12/16/2026-executive-predictions-why-the-ai-pilot-era-is-officially-over/", "https://transcarent.com/wayfinding", "https://www.navapbc.com/news/nava-ai-public-benefits", "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/payers/aetna-unveils-new-conversational-ai-navigation-tool-members", "https://lanterncare.com/blog/how-ai-is-reshaping-benefits-strategy/", "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT07474584", "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.29893", "https://www.mediontech.com/2025-healthcare-ai-revolution-it-doesnt-replace-doctors-it-gives-them-superpowers/amp/"], "chars": 1542, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note:\n\n---\n\nMahesh Venkatagiri holds a VP-level role at what was Accolade — now fully absorbed into Transcarent following a $621M acquisition completed in April 2025. The combined entity is no small integration project: it now serves over 20 million members and more than 1,700 employer and health plan clients. The strategic logic is explicitly AI-first — Transcarent's AI-powered WayFinding and specialized Care Experiences are being combined with Accolade's proven expertise in health advocacy, expert medical opinions, and virtual primary care. Operationally, this means the organization is in active mid-integration mode, pressure-testing how AI actually performs at enterprise scale rather than in controlled pilots. Their shared investment in AI has already produced tools like Accolade's True Health Actions, which generate personalized care plans using data from health records, employers, and health plans to guide member outreach and care coordination. This context aligns squarely with a post about successful AI pilots in healthcare: the Transcarent/Accolade organization has bet its entire post-merger identity on moving AI from pilot to production. As GE HealthCare's Chief Science Officer noted, \"provider AI spend increasingly moved from pilots to platforms\" in 2025. A strong opening question for a rep: **How is the team thinking about measuring the ROI of AI pilots that were scoped under the old Accolade structure, now that the platform is being unified under Transcarent's WayFinding model?**"}
