{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-ff3acbe0007e", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741254.1041033, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 14669.4, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 15063, "output_tokens": 512, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 15, "source_urls": ["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1636422/000163642226000006/jan2026investorpresentat.htm", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/news/health-catalyst-leaders-share-2025-predictions", "https://www.hcinnovationgroup.com/finance-revenue-cycle/article/55390276/health-catalyst-sells-vitalware-to-double-down-on-ai-strategy", "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1636422/000163642225000010/healthcatalyst_jpmorganm.htm", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/news/time-names-health-catalyst-among-the-worlds-leading-healthtech-innovators", "https://www.healthcatalyst.com/news/has-25-recap-charting-the-path-to-healthcare-improvement", "https://healthcatalystinc.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/health-catalyst-announces-strategic-partnership-microsoft", "https://hmacademy.com/the-ai-catalyst", "https://www.chiefhealthcareexecutive.com/view/ai-in-health-care-26-leaders-offer-predictions-for-2026", "https://www.nethealth.com/blog/2025-insights-2026-impact-ai-human-center/", "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/12/16/2026-executive-predictions-why-the-ai-pilot-era-is-officially-over/", "https://www.apexon.com/blog/2026-and-the-end-of-ai-pilots-scaling-intelligent-systems-in-hcls/", "https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/healthcare-information-technology/ai/700-lives-100m-saved-healthcare-ai-roi-in-25/", "https://opala.com/news/ai-in-healthcare-what-to-expect-in-2026/", "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.15630"], "chars": 1650, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Govardhan Terli at Health Catalyst:\n\n---\n\nHealth Catalyst is in the middle of a deliberate strategic reset squarely focused on AI. The company spent 2025 reshaping its leadership team, expanding strategic partnerships, and launching new AI-enabled products, including forging an AI partnership with Microsoft and acquiring patient engagement company Upfront Healthcare Services. Its flagship Ignite Intelligence platform combines shared models, AI agents, benchmarks, and comparison services, with Clinical Cost Intelligence moving healthcare costing from months of analysis to instant insights using ML-driven variation analysis and LLM-enabled opportunity screening. Health Catalyst has also committed to prioritizing the utilization of AI across its internal teams in 2026. This positions the company squarely inside the broader industry tension our post addresses: by the end of 2025, many healthcare organizations had dozens of AI pilots live yet only a small subset could demonstrate a measurable clinical or financial outcome, shifting the core question from \"how do we try AI?\" to \"how do we run AI as critical infrastructure?\" As a data-and-analytics vendor whose value proposition is built on measurable improvement for provider organizations, Health Catalyst is both subject to this pressure and selling into it. A strong opening question for a first conversation: **How is Health Catalyst helping its provider clients move their AI deployments from successful pilots into sustained, board-defensible outcomes at scale — and what does that transition look like internally for their own AI investments?**"}
