{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "mcp_tool_result", "ts": 1787741260.8877199, "tool": "get_lead_profile", "attempt": 1, "kind": "object", "keys": ["company_hs_id", "company_resolved", "contact_hs_id", "found", "profile", "warnings"], "result_preview": "{'found': True, 'profile': {'employee_id': 'E00016', 'company_id': 'C0016', 'decision_maker_flag': 'Yes', 'job_title': 'Managing Director', 'email': None, 'phone': '+1 (469) 850-0314', 'firstname': 'Kodanda', 'lastname': 'Naveen', 'industry': 'HEALTHCARE', 'annual_revenue_m': '11.5', 'frequency_of_purchase': 'Monthly', 'lead_context': \"**â\\x9a\\xa0ï¸\\x8f Editorial note before the lead_context note:**\\n\\nThere is a significant mismatch between the published post and the lead's context worth flagging. The Spring Blog post is a developer-ecosystem newsletter (Spring Framework/Java) with a feature on implementing *multitenancy* â\\x80\\x94 a backend software architecture topic. Innovaccer's Kodanda Naveen is a Managing Director at a healthcare AI company. The post is not healthcare-specific, and the connection is indirect at best. The note below is grounded only in what the search confirms, connecting multitenancy architecture â\\x80\\x94 the post's core theme â\\x80\\x94 to Innovaccer's actual platform situation as honestly as possible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**lead_context note:**\\n\\nInnovaccer was named a Leader in the inaugural 2026 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Healthcare Provider Industry Cloud Platforms, underscoring its position as enterprise infrastructure for health systems. Its Gravity platform unifies clinical, claims, financial, and operational data from across the enterprise and deploys AI agents that execute work across those workflows. Innovaccer is committing $250 million to expand this AI agent platform, automating workflows across prior authorization, revenue cycle management, and population health. In January 2026 it also launched Atlas, a Population Health Operating System that orchestrates data, AI, and care delivery into a unified experience across all populations and payment models. At this scale â\\x80\\x94 serving health systems, payers, and provider groups simultaneously â\\x80\\x94 multitenancy architecture is a live engineering concern: the stakes in healthcare are higher than in generic SaaS, because platforms must isolate Protected Health Information across organizational boundaries under HIPAA, where enforcement actions can reach into the millions. The tenancy model a platform chooses determines its compliance ceiling, performance floor, and infrastructure cost curve for the life of the platform â\\x80\\x94 and most healthcare SaaS teams discover this too late. A strong opening question for a first conversation: *As Innovaccer scales Gravity and Atlas across increasingly diverse health system and payer tenants, how is the engineering team currently managing data isolation and compliance boundaries without multiplying infrastructure costs?*\", 'voice_status': None, 'email_status': None, 'probability': '2', 'last_modified_voice': None, 'last_modified_email': '2026-08-25T12:29:18.216Z', 'company_name': 'Innovaccer', 'industry_group': 'Healthcare Data Platform / Population Health', 'about_us': 'Offers an AI-driven healthcare cloud that unifies data and deploys agents across clinical, operational, and financial workflows including population health, care management, and revenue cycle.', 'website_url': 'https://innovaccer.com'}, 'contact_hs_id': '534035230400', 'company_hs_id': '339352250053', 'company_resolved': True, 'warnings': []}"}
