{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741300.4952621, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 14354.2, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 15220, "output_tokens": 528, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 15, "source_urls": ["https://www.axiomlaw.com/blog/topic/global", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/resources/press-releases", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/blog/topic/healthcare-life-sciences", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/industries/healthcare", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/axiom-and-legora-mark-one-year-of-delivering-ai-enabled-legal-services-at-scale-for-in-house-legal-teams-302803178.html", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/what-we-do", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/solutions", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/faq", "https://www.jimersonfirm.com/blog/2026/02/healthcare-ai-regulation-2025-new-compliance-requirements-every-provider-must-know/", "https://www.law360.com/articles/2415514/the-high-stakes-healthcare-ai-battles-to-watch-in-2026", "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2026/05/states-continue-efforts-to-regulate-ai-in-healthcare", "https://www.aoshearman.com/en/insights/ao-shearman-on-life-sciences/ai-in-healthcare-legal-and-ethical-considerations-at-the-new-frontier", "https://practiceguides.chambers.com/practice-guides/healthcare-ai-2026", "https://healthlawblog.dwlaw.com/2026/08/the-state-of-ai-regulation-in-healthcare-still-complicated/"], "chars": 1500, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Mahesh Puliganti at Axiom Law:\n\n---\n\nAxiom Law is directly in the eye of the healthcare AI pilot story. Shared client results across healthcare show that the combination of Legora's purpose-built legal AI and Axiom's AI-enabled legal talent is delivering faster turnarounds and significant cost savings for in-house legal teams managing high-volume work. Most concretely, Axiom deployed an AI-enabled senior lawyer who used Legora to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company ahead of a product launch, saving the client 70% compared to outside counsel costs. This is a live proof point, not a hypothetical — Axiom has already run and won an AI pilot in healthcare. At the same time, the regulatory environment around healthcare AI is intensifying: there are 177 pending bills in 31 states relating to AI use in healthcare, and Axiom's own 2025 AI study reveals only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases, creating dangerous competency gaps. Puliganti, as President, sits at the intersection of Axiom's AI Tech+Talent positioning and the healthcare sector's urgent demand for compliant, proven AI solutions — making the published post's \"successful AI pilot\" theme highly resonant for his growth agenda. A good opening question: *When Axiom pitches AI-enabled legal services to healthcare clients today, what does a successful pilot look like to them — and where does the conversation most often stall?*"}
