{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-ff3acbe0007e", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741303.797243, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 15804.2, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 16008, "output_tokens": 578, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 18, "source_urls": ["https://innovaccer.com/news/black-book-recognizes-innovaccer-as-a-2026-leader-in-ai-powered-revenue-cycle-autonomy-and-population-health-data-activation", "https://innovaccer.com/resources/news/ai-trends-in-healthcare-2025-and-beyond", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260127402414/en/Innovaccer-Unveils-AI-Platforms-as-Healthcare-Leaders-Debate-Economics-Workforce-Constraints-and-Administrative-Burden-at-Xccelerate-2026", "https://innovaccer.com/resources/webinars/ai-trends-in-healthcare-2025-shaping-the-future-of-care-delivery", "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/ai-and-machine-learning/innovaccer-introduces-ai-agents-providers-automate-scheduling-patient", "https://innovaccer.com/news/ai-trends-in-healthcare-2025-and-beyond", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20251028190685/en/Innovaccer-Brings-Multimodal-AI-to-the-Frontlines-of-Care-with-NVIDIA", "https://distilinfo.com/2026/03/06/innovaccer-healthcare-ai-himss-2025/", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260402854770/en", "https://www.apexon.com/blog/2026-and-the-end-of-ai-pilots-scaling-intelligent-systems-in-hcls/", "https://healthtechdigital.com/the-ai-implementation-gap-why-80-of-healthcare-ai-projects-fail-to-scale-beyond-pilot-phase/", "https://www.healthcareitnews.com/news/asia/not-all-ai-pilots-will-scale", "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12894408/", "https://premierinc.com/newsroom/blog/the-ai-wild-west-is-over-why-2026-is-the-year-health-systems-must-take-control", "https://hitconsultant.net/2025/12/16/2026-executive-predictions-why-the-ai-pilot-era-is-officially-over/", "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.00839", "https://www.healthcareitnews.com/news/healthcare-cios-see-ai-integration-competitive-necessity", "https://www.healthcareittoday.com/2026/04/24/barriers-to-scaling-ai-initiatives-and-effective-strategies-to-overcome-them/"], "chars": 1739, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Kodanda Naveen at Innovaccer:\n\n---\n\nInnovaccer is one of the most prominent vendors in the AI-driven healthcare data space right now. Black Book Research ranked Innovaccer #1 in both AI-Powered Revenue Cycle Autonomy and Population Health Data Integration in its 2026 evaluations, recognizing its leadership in autonomous, agentic AI with measurable real-world execution and operational fit. It also achieved Best in KLAS scores across three categories in the 2026 awards, covering Data Analytics for Providers, Data Analytics for Payers, and CRM Platforms. This makes the post's theme — what makes an AI pilot truly succeed — land with particular force here, because Innovaccer is now in the business of helping health systems move *past* pilots. At its Xccelerate 2026 conference, healthcare executives gathered to address how to meet rising care demand with constrained workforce supply, tightening margins, and increasing administrative complexity, and leaders discussed how economic pressure and operational inefficiency are forcing organizations to rethink how work gets done. A key tension Innovaccer itself surfaces is whether AI autonomy becomes embedded standard work rather than a parallel tool that staff work around. Meanwhile, industry data shows only 4% of health systems have scaled AI with measurable outcomes, while 45% cite difficulty scaling pilots — precisely the gap Innovaccer's platform is designed to close. A strong opening question for a first conversation: **When Innovaccer's customers move from an AI pilot to enterprise-wide deployment, where do they most commonly hit friction — is it data unification, workflow adoption, or demonstrating measurable ROI to the C-suite?**"}
