{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-0168b546d373", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741321.7063448, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 15074.8, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 16759, "output_tokens": 525, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 18, "source_urls": ["https://www.cedar.com/all-press/cedar-unveils-agentic-ai-purpose-built-for-healthcare-billing-aiming-to-help-providers-cut-costs-with-a-30-reduction-in-patient-billing-calls", "https://www.cedar.com/all-press/cedar-expands-ai-powered-personalization-in-healthcare-billing-with-new-cedar-intelligence-capabilities", "https://www.cedar.com/all-press/cedar-builds-ai-powered-tools-to-improve-healthcare-financial-experience-for-patients-across-the-united-states-in-collaboration-with-google-cloud", "https://www.techtarget.com/revcyclemanagement/news/366641613/Cedar-goes-beyond-propensity-to-pay-to-bolster-patient-billing", "https://www.cedar.com/", "https://www.cedar.com/press", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cedar-unveils-year-in-review-and-vision-ahead-report-showcasing-bold-advancements-in-tackling-healthcare-affordability-302357982.html", "https://www.healthcarefinancenews.com/news/cedar-announces-agentic-ai-healthcare-billing", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cedar-unveils-agentic-ai-purpose-built-for-healthcare-billing-aiming-to-help-providers-cut-costs-with-a-30-reduction-in-patient-billing-calls-302440435.html", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cedar-expands-ai-powered-personalization-in-healthcare-billing-with-new-cedar-intelligence-capabilities-302736567.html", "https://www.hfma.org/revenue-cycle/the-revenue-cycle-of-the-future-ai-boom-and-workflow-redesigns-accelerate-rev-cycle-transformation/", "https://blog.nym.health/ai-in-healthcare-revenue-cycle-management", "https://www.notablehealth.com/blog/ai-and-automation-in-revenue-cycle-management-must-know-trends-for-2025", "https://www.hfma.org/technology/most-healthcare-organizations-are-adopting-ai-in-the-revenue-cycle-hfma-poll/", "https://www.waystar.com/insights-resources/resources-page/report-top-6-trends-for-healthcare-revenue-cycle-2025/", "https://www.ey.com/en_us/insights/health/ai-driven-rcm-in-healthcare", "https://www.aspirion.com/the-year-ai-transformed-revenue-cycle-2025-insights-and-2026-predictions/", "https://www.outsourcestrategies.com/blog/beyond-billing-how-ai-reshaping-healthcare-revenue-cycle/"], "chars": 1616, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Austin Terry at Cedar:\n\n---\n\nCedar is itself an AI-native player in the healthcare patient financial experience space, so the theme of a successful AI pilot lands with particular resonance here — they are both a potential customer story and a peer validator. Cedar recently announced a major expansion of Cedar Intelligence, its AI-powered decision engine, which draws on healthcare-specific data to analyze more than 80 patient attributes and personalize billing experiences at scale. The company has also launched Kora, an AI voice agent projected to automate 30% of inbound billing calls, trained on Cedar's pre-existing billing data to answer patient questions beyond traditional IVR. This makes Cedar acutely aware of what it takes to move AI from pilot to production — and the credibility gaps that can stall that journey. Across the broader healthcare finance market, HFMA data shows AI pilots are beginning to move to production-scale deployments, with 53% of healthcare finance professionals currently conducting pilots in select areas. Cedar's provider clients are also navigating a sharp payer-mix shift following the One Big Beautiful Bill Act, with 10 million additional patients expected to lose coverage through 2034, increasing self-pay volume and collections pressure. A strong opening question for a first conversation: *When Cedar has gone to its own provider clients to make the case for scaling an AI pilot, what has been the hardest part of proving the ROI internally — and is that a challenge Cedar itself faced when rolling out Kora or Cedar Intelligence?*"}
