{"stream": "process", "run_id": "res-ff3acbe0007e", "event": "model_response", "ts": 1787741326.6448197, "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "duration_ms": 15435.1, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "input_tokens": 15220, "output_tokens": 610, "web_search_requests": 2, "searches": 2, "sources": 15, "source_urls": ["https://www.axiomlaw.com/blog/topic/global", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/resources/press-releases", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/blog/topic/healthcare-life-sciences", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/industries/healthcare", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/axiom-and-legora-mark-one-year-of-delivering-ai-enabled-legal-services-at-scale-for-in-house-legal-teams-302803178.html", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/what-we-do", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/solutions", "https://www.axiomlaw.com/faq", "https://www.jimersonfirm.com/blog/2026/02/healthcare-ai-regulation-2025-new-compliance-requirements-every-provider-must-know/", "https://www.law360.com/articles/2415514/the-high-stakes-healthcare-ai-battles-to-watch-in-2026", "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2026/05/states-continue-efforts-to-regulate-ai-in-healthcare", "https://www.aoshearman.com/en/insights/ao-shearman-on-life-sciences/ai-in-healthcare-legal-and-ethical-considerations-at-the-new-frontier", "https://practiceguides.chambers.com/practice-guides/healthcare-ai-2026", "https://healthlawblog.dwlaw.com/2026/08/the-state-of-ai-regulation-in-healthcare-still-complicated/"], "chars": 1837, "text_preview": "Here is the `lead_context` note for Mahesh Puliganti at Axiom Law:\n\n---\n\nAxiom Law is a natural fit for a conversation about successful AI pilots in healthcare legal work. Shared client results across healthcare, aerospace, real estate, and manufacturing show that the combination of Legora's purpose-built legal AI and Axiom's AI-enabled legal talent is delivering faster turnarounds, cleaner data, and significant cost savings for in-house legal teams managing high-volume legal work. A standout proof point is directly on-theme: Axiom deployed an AI-enabled senior lawyer who used Legora to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company, migrating hundreds of agreements ahead of a product launch, and the client saved 70% compared to the cost of sending the work to outside counsel. Meanwhile, the broader healthcare industry context reinforces urgency — 46% of U.S. healthcare organizations are currently implementing generative AI technologies, yet Axiom's own 2025 AI study reveals only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases, creating a meaningful gap that Axiom's model is positioned to close. Regulatory complexity is compounding the challenge: states moved aggressively to enact laws governing the use of AI in healthcare in 2024 and 2025, and this trend has continued into 2026, with state legislatures enacting laws regulating AI's role in clinical decision-making, patient care, and broader healthcare operations. Puliganti, as President, would own the go-to-market and client strategy for how Axiom positions and scales these AI-enabled healthcare offerings. A strong opening question for a first call: **What does a successful AI pilot look like from Axiom's side — and what's the biggest barrier healthcare clients face in moving from pilot to scaled deployment?**"}
